  CHAIN[powers_and_abilities]: "are nullified, along with healing, the slowing of movement speed, and the ability to double jump. Staying here too long results in death. *Take: Oryx’s favored ability is an ontological weapon, or ontopathogenic to be more precise, meaning it infects the very existence of things. It is heavily implied to be the inspiration of the Gorgon's Gaze, another ontological weapon. The ability to Take involves conducting a mathematical operation on the target and reforming matter in a self-contained reality, where the creator defines past, present, and future, imposing a singular origin and all decision"
  CHAIN[weaknesses]: 'Failing to live up to his nature of understanding and curiosity as well as failing to uphold his tithe of death to his worm will result in his eventual consumption. Killing him in his own throne world makes it much harder, though not impossible, for him to return.'
